    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step1.Button" xml:space="preserve">Open openrouter.ai</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step1.Text" xml:space="preserve">OpenRouter is a gateway to models from many vendors: one account and one key for all of them.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step1.Title" xml:space="preserve">Sign up at openrouter.ai</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step2.Text" xml:space="preserve">Models are paid from your account balance; top it up in the Credits section. The app shows an estimate for the next answer next to the context ring.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step2.Title" xml:space="preserve">Add credits</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step3.Button" xml:space="preserve">Open OpenRouter keys</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step3.Limit" xml:space="preserve">You can give the key a spending limit on OpenRouter's side, a second safeguard next to the app's own limits on the Key &amp; Info page.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step3.Text" xml:space="preserve">On the keys page, create a new key and copy it right away.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step3.Title" xml:space="preserve">Create a key</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step4.Text" xml:space="preserve">On the Key &amp; Info page press Add key, choose OpenRouter and paste the key; it is stored encrypted by Windows. The OPENROUTER_API_KEY environment variable also works, and then the app keeps no copy.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step4.Title" xml:space="preserve">Add the key to the app</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step5.Text" xml:space="preserve">The model picker gets an OpenRouter column. Every model slot has its own provider and key. Variants marked :batch cost half as much but answer through a queue, which takes minutes.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step5.Title" xml:space="preserve">Pick models</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="S.Info.Or.Step5.VeniceOnly" xml:space="preserve">Image generation and page reading exist only at Venice; without a Venice key those tools refuse.</system:String>
